Hexagon HTP: the fused matvec reads src2 from DDR, and the host fuses only the whole product

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches of patches/series before this one.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/matmul-ops.c  the src2 read of the two matvec kernels
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp  the conditions of try_fuse_mul_mat_add

The DSP library and the host library both change.

Defect 1: the aligned src2 load of the matvec kernels

With op fusion on, the host fuses MUL_MAT and ADD when the activation has one row.
The kernel for one row copies the ADD input (src2) with DMA into VTCM. The copy
starts at the byte offset of the first row of the thread. Then the kernel adds
the slice with hvx_add_f32_uaa, which loads src2 with aligned vector loads.

The F16 and F32 matvec kernel (hvx_mv_2d) splits the rows per thread in even
counts, not in multiples of 32. Thus, the slice of thread 1 and of each later
thread starts at an offset that is not a multiple of 128 bytes. The aligned
load ignores the low bits of the address, and the thread reads the wrong bias.

The Qwen3.5 graph adds ssm_dt.bias to the output of the 16-row ssm_alpha
matrix (src/models/qwen35.cpp, line 378). That matrix is F32 in the Q4_0 file
and F16 in the F16 file, thus it always takes hvx_mv_2d. With 4 or 6 threads,
rows 4 thru 15 get the bias of rows 0 thru 3. The decay gate of the gated
delta net is wrong, and the text after the first token is not correct.

Prefill is correct. The fusion at m > 1 needs the HMX path (ggml-hexagon.cpp,
line 2632), and a 16-row matrix never takes the HMX path (line 4257).

Fix

The two matvec kernels read src2 from DDR with unaligned loads in the final
add (hvx_add_f32_uau). The m > 1 kernel already does this in
hvx_tensor_add_f32_grid. The DMA copy of src2 is removed, and with it the
dma_queue_pop_nowait that never waited for the copy. The VTCM layout does not
change, thus the host and the DSP stay in sync.

Defect 2: the host fused a product that the ADD does not read whole

try_fuse_mul_mat_add fused a MUL_MAT and the ADD after it when one input of the ADD
had the data address of the product. Two conditions give an incorrect fused op:

- The ADD reads the product through a view with fewer rows or columns at the same
  address. The fused kernel writes the full product into the smaller output of the
  ADD, thus it writes past that output.
- The other input of the ADD (src2 of the fused op) has a broadcast in dimension 0,
  or a dimension that ggml_add repeats. The fused kernels read full rows of src2 and
  broadcast only a dimension of size 1, thus they read past src2.

The host fuses the two ops only when the ADD reads the whole product (the same
address, type, shape and strides), the output of the ADD has the shape of the
product, and src2 has full rows and, in each other dimension, a size of 1 or the
size of the product. The matcher is upstream code.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
index 3f14956..c281192 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp
@@ -2614,14 +2614,35 @@ struct ggml_hexagon_opbatch {
 
         if (!ggml_hexagon_tensor_is_fuseable(mm_out)) return false;
 
+        // The ADD must read the whole product: the product itself, or a view with the same bytes,
+        // type, shape and strides. A view with fewer rows or columns starts at the same address,
+        // but the fused kernel writes the full product into the smaller output of the ADD.
+        auto is_whole_product = [mm_out](const ggml_tensor * t) {
+            return t == mm_out || (t->data == mm_out->data && t->type == mm_out->type &&
+                                   ggml_are_same_shape(t, mm_out) && ggml_are_same_stride(t, mm_out));
+        };
         const ggml_tensor * src2;
-        if (add_src0 == mm_out || add_src0->data == mm_out->data) {
+        if (is_whole_product(add_src0)) {
             src2 = add_src1;
-        } else if (add_src1 == mm_out || add_src1->data == mm_out->data) {
+        } else if (is_whole_product(add_src1)) {
             src2 = add_src0;
         } else {
             return false;
         }
+        if (!ggml_are_same_shape(node.dst(), mm_out)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        // The fused kernels read full rows of src2 (ne[0] of the product) and broadcast only a
+        // dimension of size 1 (htp/matmul-ops.c:359, 472 and 3664-3667). ggml_add also permits a
+        // broadcast in dimension 0 and a repeat of a larger size, which the kernels read outside src2.
+        if (src2->ne[0] != mm_out->ne[0]) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        for (int i = 1; i < GGML_MAX_DIMS; i++) {
+            if (src2->ne[i] != 1 && src2->ne[i] != mm_out->ne[i]) {
+                return false;
+            }
+        }
 
         const ggml_tensor * src0 = last_node.src0();
         const ggml_tensor * src1 = last_node.src1();
